  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "game-description-228f16dd-d582-48b9-a987-a0c996442fac-0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "This entry uses Football to mean American football, since association football has its own Soccer entry. Two teams attempt to advance an oval ball into the opponent’s end zone, using runs and passes while a defense tries to stop them. The offense normally has four downs to gain ten yards and renew its opportunity to keep possession."
    },
    {
      "id": "game-description-228f16dd-d582-48b9-a987-a0c996442fac-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "The sport developed from nineteenth-century rugby and football traditions in the United States. Walter Camp was an important contributor to rules such as the line of scrimmage and the downs system, but it was not a one-person invention. Play combines specialized roles, rehearsed formations, and decisions made under pressure."
    },
